+## v1.7.1 addendum (23.09.2026)
+
+Schema version stays "1.7" (the app's version gate already accepts it); the file
+`measurement-v1.7.json` is extended in place. Still additive.
+
+Why: the Braamheide run (schema 1.7) raised `VALIDATION: WL-5: parent_attachment_id
+is only valid on roof faces` - the model wanted to say "this WALL belongs to the
+dormer", which is exactly what the viewer needs to place an attachment's walls and
+windows. The same run raised a false `geometry check eave total: model 25000 vs
+derived 18600 (34% off)`: the measured eaves include dormer, canopy and addition
+eaves, while the check compares against the main roof only. v1.7 linked roof FACES
+to attachments but not walls and not edges.
+
+Changes:
+1. `faces[].parent_attachment_id` is now valid on wall faces too (roof face = the
+   attachment's roof, wall face = one of its walls). Soffit/fascia still rejected.
+2. New `edges[].parent_attachment_id` (AT-n | null): the attachment an eave, rake
+   or hip belongs to.
+3. Geometry checks: edge sums (eave, ridge, rake, hip) count main-building edges
+   only - edges naming an attachment are skipped. Roof-area and pitch statistics
+   already skipped attachment facets since v1.7.
+4. Validation: parent_attachment_id on faces and edges must name an existing
+   attachment; on a face it must be a roof or wall face.
+5. Extraction prompts (all three): the ATTACHMENT ROOF RULE now also asks for the
+   id on the attachment's wall faces and roof edges; openings keep parent_face_id.
+6. Fixture: garage walls WL-5/WL-6 and the garage edges carry AT-7.
